From 9264078cc33e8ab699f0b27901fda9e29441d3dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Fischer <info@tobiasfischer.info>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:50:23 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Port from PyQt5 to PySide6 (Qt 6)

PyQt5 is end-of-life and has no wheels for recent Python versions, while
PySide6 is the Qt for Python binding maintained by the Qt Company and is
what other tools that want to embed TagLab already use. Most of the diff
is mechanical (module rename, pyqtSignal/pyqtSlot -> Signal/Slot,
exec_ -> exec); the parts that needed thought are:

- QRegExp -> QRegularExpression, setFilterRegExp -> setFilterRegularExpression
- QAction moved from QtWidgets to QtGui
- QT_VERSION_STR is gone; QDesktopServices comes from QtGui
- two enums that were reached through the instance (AnimatedDocks,
  AnchorViewCenter) now use their scoped names
- Project.save() dumped self.__dict__, which under PySide6 also contains
  the bound SignalInstance objects; they are filtered out before json.dumps
- QtAlignmentToolWidget used the PyQt5-only QOpenGLFunctions_2_0 private
  module. It now uses QOpenGLVersionFunctionsFactory, defines the few GL
  constants it needs (the Qt6 bindings do not expose them), uploads vertex
  data through a QOpenGLBuffer (raw client pointers cannot be passed),
  makes the context current before creating textures, and sets sampler
  and float uniforms with setUniformValue1i/1f (an int would otherwise be
  sent as an unsigned and ignored by the GLSL 1.20 shaders).
  Checked by rendering the alpha-blend preview on a real Cocoa window.

install.py, install_conda_windows.py, dependencies.md and the README now
say pyside6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
